{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "MAL",
  "chapter": 3,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "MAL.3.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAL.3.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, I will send my messenger, and he shall prepare the way before me: and the LORD, whom ye seek, will suddenly come to his temple, even the messenger of the covenant, whom ye delight in: behold, he will come, saith the LORD of hosts.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "MAL.3.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAL.3.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But who may abide the day of his coming? and who shall stand when he appeareth? for he ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " like a refiner's fire, and like fuller's soap.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAL.3.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAL.3.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he shall sit ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a refiner and purifier of silver: and he shall purify the sons of Levi, and purge them as gold and silver, that they may offer to the LORD an offering in righteousness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAL.3.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAL.3.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then shall the offering of Judah and Jerusalem be pleasant to the LORD, as in the days of old, and as in former years.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAL.3.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAL.3.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And I will come near to you to judgment; and I will be a swift witness against the sorcerers, and against the adulterers, and against false swearers, and against those that oppress the hireling in ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " wages, the widow, and the fatherless, and that turn aside the stranger ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "from his right",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and fear not me, saith the LORD of hosts.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAL.3.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAL.3.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the LORD, I change not; therefore ye sons of Jacob are not consumed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAL.3.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAL.3.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Even from the days of your fathers ye have gone away from my ordinances, and have not kept ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ". Return to me, and I will return to you, saith the LORD of hosts. But ye said, In what shall we return?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAL.3.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAL.3.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Will a man rob God? yet ye have robbed me. But ye say, In what have we robbed thee? In tithes and offerings.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAL.3.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAL.3.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Ye ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " cursed with a curse: for ye have robbed me, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " this whole nation.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAL.3.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAL.3.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Bring ye all the tithes into the store-house, that there may be food in my house, and prove me now with this, saith the LORD of hosts, if I will not open you the windows of heaven, and pour you out a blessing, that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there shall",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be room",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " enough ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to receive it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAL.3.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAL.3.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And I will rebuke the devourer for your sakes, and he shall not destroy the fruits of your ground; neither shall your vine cast her fruit before the time in the field, saith the LORD of hosts.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAL.3.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAL.3.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And all nations shall call you blessed: for ye shall be a delightsome land, saith the LORD of hosts.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAL.3.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAL.3.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Your words have been stout against me, saith the LORD. Yet ye say, What have we spoken ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "so much",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " against thee?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAL.3.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAL.3.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Ye have said, It ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " vain to serve God: and what profit ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that we have kept his ordinance, and that we have walked mournfully before the LORD of hosts?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAL.3.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAL.3.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And now we call the proud happy; yes, they that work wickedness are set up; even ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "they that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " tempt God are delivered.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAL.3.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAL.3.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then they that feared the LORD spoke often one to another: and the LORD hearkened, and heard ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and a book of remembrance was written before him for them that feared the LORD, and that thought upon his name.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAL.3.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAL.3.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they shall be mine, saith the LORD of hosts, in that day when I make up my jewels; and I will spare them, as a man spareth his own son that serveth him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAL.3.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAL.3.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then shall ye return and discern between the righteous and the wicked, between him that serveth God and him that serveth him not.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
